# UST.G3BY Selected G3BI H02 Exact Update Rank

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_UNIFORM_UPDATE_RANK`

## Theorem

On the unique `24,767`-dimensional corrected G3BI H02 DM core, write

```text
A(gamma) = B0 + gamma B1 + ... + gamma^5 B5
```

and form the horizontal uniform update matrix

```text
H = [B1 B2 B3 B4 B5].
```

After removing identically constant columns, `H` has shape
`24,767 x 88,380` and `7,908,830` nonzero entries. Its support graph has
maximum matching size `14,419`, proving

```text
rank_Q(H) <= 14,419.
```

The matching selects a `14,419 x 14,419` integer coefficient minor. Exact
sparse factorization gives

```text
det(minor) = 10432 mod 21817.
```

The integer determinant is therefore nonzero, so reduction gives the equal
lower bound. Consequently

```text
rank_Q(H) = 14,419.
```

## Consequence

The corrected H02 endpoint admits a uniform Woodbury presentation of exact
dimension `14,419`, improving the prior active-row bound `15,158` by `739`
directions. This rank is minimal for a generic coefficient-level update space;
further reduction must use the selected source-reachable action rather than a
smaller universal update basis.

The independent root difference `A(1971)-A(5)` has structural rank only
`14,189`; it is a useful specialized screen but is not used for the exact
uniform rank proof.

## Boundary

The theorem does not evaluate the `14,419`-square Woodbury kernel, construct
the initial rank-42 homology-to-de-Rham coordinates, perform integral
Gauss-Manin transport, or emit the terminal `248`-coordinate readout.

